> [This] program is designed for endocrinologists,[ diabetes] and metabolism specialists, family[ medicine] physicians, internists, physician assistants, nurse practitioners, nurses,[ diet]itians and other interested professionals.
The last few years have witnessed some of the greatest[ breakthrough]s[ in diabetes] management since the discovery of insulin. We have gone from two classes of drugs[ for] glycemic control to 14 classes. Gluco-centricity is also being placed in its[ correct] perspective and personalized medicine has replaced it with a multifactorial regimen, addressing the complexity of risk that accompanies[ diabetes].[ For the] first time we have real compounds that reduce cardiovascular events and even combat[ congest]ive heart failure.[ There] is now a new recognition of the relationship between[ hypertension] and renal dysfunction that compromises cardiac function. We have finally conceded that insulin resistance should surrender its crown and that the[ central] role of beta cell function be given the[ recognition] it deserves. Please join us for this one day[ diabetes] conference[ at] Eastern Virginia Medical School.[]


